the target language is: lps.

% turns.le — the clock: Inform's turn as a layer over LPS cycles.
%
% This is optional. A story that includes it gets `the turn begins` and `the
% turn ends`, which the player (src/edges/lps_play.pl) injects around each
% command — the command with the first, and the second once the cycle has
% settled — and `the turn is N`, which counts them. An every-turn rule keys on
% `the turn ends`; a scheduled event names a turn. A story that does not
% include it is driven the same way, without the markers: a command goes in,
% the session runs to quiescence, and the prompt comes back. alice.le uses
% the turn; alice_pure_lps.le is the same story without it.
%
%     the knowledge base my story includes these resources: world, turns.

the events are:
    the turn begins; known as begin_turn.
    the turn ends; known as end_turn.

the fluents are:
    the turn is *a number*; known as turn.

the knowledge base turns includes:

when the turn begins
then the turn that is a number becomes number + 1.
